From d69add475b165f664e286422c58fc31c2ae9fdfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] param-spec, rend-spec: Document HSDir and BEGIN_DIR DoS
 parameters

Add the "DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled", "DoSBeginDirMaxStreams",
"HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit" and "HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop" consensus
parameters, and note that HSV3MaxDescriptorSize also bounds the request
body a non-authority directory server will buffer. In rend-spec, state
that each descriptor fetch and upload is made on its own circuit, that
HSDirs may close or refuse requests that break this or come from an
unknown previous hop, or rate-limit fetches, and that clients should
then try another HSDir.

Companion to tor#41339.
---
 spec/param-spec.md              | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md | 11 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spec/param-spec.md b/spec/param-spec.md
index 6a86178..9d7a532 100644
--- a/spec/param-spec.md
+++ b/spec/param-spec.md
@@ -347,6 +347,11 @@ will upload its descriptor to.
 Min: 1. Max: 128. Default: 4
 
 "HSV3MaxDescriptorSize" -- Maximum descriptor size (in bytes).
+On relays that are not directory authorities, this also bounds the body of
+an HTTP request that the directory server will buffer: once a request body
+reaches this many bytes (or 16 MB, if that is smaller), the request is
+rejected before more of it is buffered. Directory authorities keep the
+16 MB limit.
 Min: 1. Max: INT32_MAX. Default: 50000
 
 "hs_service_max_rdv_failures" -- This parameter determines the
@@ -492,6 +497,37 @@ First appeared: 0.4.9.0-alpha-dev.
     First appeared: 0.4.9.0-alpha-dev.
 ```
 
+"DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled" -- If 1, a public relay refuses a BEGIN_DIR
+stream on a circuit that already has "DoSBeginDirMaxStreams" open
+directory streams. Tor clients treat such a refusal as a failed directory
+request. Relays count such streams whatever the value. The relay torrc
+option of the same name (0, 1, or auto) overrides this parameter.
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
+"DoSBeginDirMaxStreams" -- The maximum number of open directory streams on
+a circuit. See "DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled". A nonzero relay torrc option of
+the same name overrides this parameter.
+Min: 1. Max: INT32_MAX. Default: 64.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
+"HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit" -- If 1, a public onion service directory
+closes, with reason RESOURCELIMIT, any circuit on which it receives a
+second onion service descriptor fetch or upload. Directories count such
+circuits whatever the value. The relay torrc option of the same name (0, 1,
+or auto) overrides this parameter.
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
+"HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop" -- If 1, a public onion service directory
+refuses, with an HTTP 503 response, an onion service descriptor fetch or
+upload whose previous hop is not a relay in its consensus or for which it
+has a descriptor. Directories count such requests whatever the value. The
+relay torrc option of the same name (0, 1, or auto) overrides this
+parameter. It is independent of "refuseunknownexits".
+Min: 0. Max: 1. Default: 0.
+First appeared: TBD.
+
 <a id="param-spec.txt-10"></a>
 
 ## Padding-related parameters {#padding}
diff --git a/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md b/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
index 066f34d..2c0571c 100644
--- a/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
+++ b/spec/rend-spec/deriving-keys.md
@@ -433,6 +433,17 @@ version which is "3" in this case.
 
 These requests must be made anonymously, on circuits not used for
 anything else.
+Each descriptor fetch and each descriptor upload MUST be made on its own
+circuit: a client or service MUST NOT send a second such request on a
+circuit that already carried one.
+An onion service directory MAY close a circuit that carries more than one
+such request (see "HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit" in the
+[parameter specification](../param-spec.md)), and MAY refuse a request whose
+previous hop it does not recognize as a relay (see
+"HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop").
+It MAY also close the circuit of a fetch of a descriptor whose fetches it
+is rate-limiting.
+Clients SHOULD then try another responsible onion service directory.
 
 The legacy [".z" suffix][dot-z] is **not** supported for these URLs.
 
